    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "BANGKOK\nDONG KINGMAN",
      "Cocktailo\nSherry Dubonnet Campari\nManhattan Gin Martini Vodka Martini Vermouth\nBloody Mary Screwdriver Whiskey Sour\nTom Collins Vodka Collins Daiquiri Scotch Bourbon\nCanadian\nGin Vodka Rum Premium Beer\nMenus\nApéritif\n*\nCaviar\nFresh caviar with its traditional accompaniments\nSelected Gourmet Delicacies\nRoast au Vo\nA selected cut of aged beef, turkey or other succulent meat\nroasted on board and carved to order\nYour flight attendant will advise you of todays roast\n45;$\nE\nSliced Beef Prepared in Japanese Style with Scallions in Piquant Sauce\n** 403**\nChicken Bombay\nFillet of Sole in Lemon Butter\n* =",
      "A selected cut of aged beet, turkey or other succulent me ar\nroasted on board and carved to order\nyour tight attendant will advise you of today's roast\n7F8 |-\nSliced Beef Prepared in Japanese Style with Scallions in Piquant Sauce\n778712818\nchicken Bombay\n-illet of Sole in Lemon Butter\nPlat du Jour\nPotatoes Maison\nTossed Garden Salad\nButtered Vegetable Bouquet\nSelection of Fruits and Cheeses\nCoffee\n0-C-\nTea\nDessert\nDecaffeinated Coffee\nGreen Tea\nSelected French Wines\nFrench Champagne Brut\nDrambuie Amaretto di Saronno\nBénédictine\nCrème de Menthe\nCognac VSOP\nCointreau",
      "BANGKOK\nDong Kingman, the award winning Chinese-American artist, travels the world sketching and painting\nthe beautiful, the monumental and the picturesque. His watercolors grace more than forty\npermanent museum and private collections in the USA and abroad\nAmong the 300 splendid temples in Bangkok, the most famous are: the Temple of the Emerald\nBuddha, Temple of the Reclining Buddha, Temple of the Golden Buddha and the Temple of the Dawn.\nThe exotic oriental ambiance is heightened by the saffron robed monks seen everywhere and the\ntraditional classical dancing. Here one can dine on the best rice in the world temptingly prepared\nand laced with curry.\nThe thoughtful service and gracious accommodations offered by the luxurious Siam\nInter-Continental are especially attuned to international travelers.\nBanakok is served by Pan Am on its Round-the-World fliahts.\nOPAN AM.\n2001,080.253"
    ],
